# Commit conventions

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <description>

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

**Types:** `feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`

**Scopes:** `skills`, `hooks`, `marketplace`, `ci`, `docs`

## Examples

```
feat(skills): add pr-dev skill for persistent PR drive loop
fix(hooks): handle missing session state in capture-task-slug
docs(skills): update reference.md with plugin-compat and repo-scaffold
chore(ci): switch ubuntu runner to ubuntu-latest
```

## Rules

- One commit per logical change — never batch unrelated fixes
- Never commit with `git add .` — stage specific files to avoid secrets or build artifacts
- Never push directly to `main` — always use a feature branch and open a PR
- `make validate` must pass before committing (JSON + shellcheck + SKILL.md frontmatter)
